From b88ff527900018312a5cfab36f0ddf1e1761e860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patil Navaneeth <pnavanee@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:04:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] shikra: enable SMMU secure register programming

Add the Shikra SMMU configuration table and enable the QTI SMMU driver
for shikra_qli, so qti_smmu_init() programs the secure SMMU registers
during BL31 platform setup.

Shikra has two SMMU instances: Apps (0x0C600000) and GPU GFX
(0x059A0000). Register addresses are from IPCat (shikra_1.0) and
values are from the Shikra SMMU HSR v2.0 (the set QTEE programs from
smmu_hsr_shikra.xml).

Per the security ownership split, only secure registers are programmed
here:
  - Apps: CUSTOM_CFG_SEC, SACR, CLOCK_GATING_SEC, client debug
    SSD_IDX (ANOC_1, MM_RT, PCIE) and SID_HALT (ANOC_1, PCIE)
  - GPU: SPARE_REG_1_SEC, CLOCK_GATING_SEC, client debug SSD_IDX,
    SID_HALT and WUSER (GFX_0)

Intentionally not programmed: non-secure CUSTOM_CFG, NSACR and GPU
TLBIS_CTRL, CBn_ACTLR (HLOS), and GPU ACR (KVM).

Changes:
  - add drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.c
  - add include/drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.h
  - add QTI_SMMU_CFG_BASE and QTI_GPU_SMMU_CFG_BASE to shikra_def.h
  - include smmu.mk from shikra_qli/platform.mk

Change-Id: Ic37e3d3564eb525b0b223a0d433004d1335a4871

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Patil Navaneeth <pnavanee@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.c           | 38 +++++++++
 include/drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.h   | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++
 plat/qti/bruin/shikra/inc/shikra_def.h       |  6 ++
 plat/qti/bruin/shikra/shikra_qli/platform.mk |  3 +-
 4 files changed, 130 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.c
 create mode 100644 include/drivers/qti/smmu/shikra/smmu_cfg.h

